25 4992 L 2125 4250 L 2118 4186 L 2118 282 L 2125 218 L 2125 -525 z\nM 1926 -13 Q 1562 -13 1258 89 Q 954 192 723 368 Q 493 544 333 762 L 710 1101 Q 851 909 1033 758 Q 1216 608 1443 525 Q 1670 442 1926 442 Q 2221 442 2451 541 Q 2682 640 2813 819 Q 2944 998 2944 1248 Q 2944 1466 2857 1616 Q 2771 1766 2585 1868 Q 2400 1971 2099 2029 L 1754 2099 Q 1318 2189 1030 2349 Q 742 2509 604 2749 Q 467 2989 467 3315 Q 467 3667 646 3926 Q 826 4186 1162 4333 Q 1498 4480 1965 4480 Q 2470 4480 2832 4275 Q 3194 4070 3424 3750 L 3034 3456 Q 2874 3680 2602 3853 Q 2330 4026 1946 4026 Q 1472 4026 1222 3834 Q 973 3642 973 3354 Q 973 3123 1069 2972 Q 1165 2822 1353 2732 Q 1542 2643 1805 2586 L 2150 2509 Q 2611 2406 2899 2246 Q 3187 2086 3318 1852 Q 3450 1619 3450 1280 Q 3450 883 3254 592 Q 3059 301 2716 144 Q 2374 -13 1926 -13 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-2a\" d=\"M 595 0 L 595 4467 L 1312 4467 L 2157 2886 L 2592 2061 L 2624 2061 L 3066 2886 L 3910 4467 L 4602 4467 L 4602 0 L 4077 0 L 4077 3014 L 4077 3763 L 4045 3763 L 3667 3014 L 2598 1069 L 1530 3014 L 1152 3763 L 1120 3763 L 1120 3014 L 1120 0 L 595 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-ae\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-2a\" transform=\"translate(59.796875 0)\"/></g></g></g><g id=\"patch_3\"><path d=\"M 56.425455 43.9296 L 196.207273 43.9296 L 196.207273 17.6 L 56.425455 17.6 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p36e5aa3d71)\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_4\"><path d=\"M 231.152727 43.9296 L 370.934545 43.9296 L 370.934545 108.9792 L 231.152727 108.9792 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#p36e5aa3d71)\" style=\"fill: #c2410c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_5\"><path d=\"M 40.7 134.99904 L 40.7 13.03104 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"patch_6\"><path d=\"M 40.7 134.99904 L 386.66 134.99904 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #c9d1dc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"text_7\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(120.428239 15.4) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\" d=\"M 3501 0 L 563 0 L 563 474 L 1811 474 L 1811 4070 L 1766 4070 L 640 3021 L 326 3360 L 1510 4467 L 2349 4467 L 2349 474 L 3501 474 L 3501 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" d=\"M 870 -77 Q 672 -77 576 28 Q 480 134 480 294 L 480 378 Q 480 544 576 646 Q 672 749 870 749 Q 1075 749 1168 646 Q 1261 544 1261 378 L 1261 294 Q 1261 134 1168 28 Q 1075 -77 870 -77 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-41\" d=\"M 1696 0 L 1120 0 L 2829 4006 L 922 4006 L 922 3174 L 442 3174 L 442 4467 L 3373 4467 L 3373 3994 L 1696 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-41\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_8\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(292.755511 117.1792) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-90\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3c\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p36e5aa3d71\"><rect x=\"40.7\" y=\"13.03104\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"121.968\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · NPV ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Cash flow falls to $1.1M a year. NPV = −$15M + $1.1M × 9.82 = <b>−$4.2M</b>.</p> <p>Break-even: gate fees can fall to about 86% of today's level before the project stops paying.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> the project's value depends on gate fees, which are not contracted and face new competition.</p>"},{"q":"What would you need before saying yes?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Long-term waste contracts</b> (10+ years) for most of the gate-fee income, at fees above 86% of today's</li> <li>Use more of the co-op's own manure and crop waste, so less depends on outside food waste</li> <li>A fixed electricity price contract if available</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Build the digester only once most of its waste is under long-term contract. The base case NPV is about +$1.7M, but gate fees are 40% of income, uncontracted, and likely to fall as three new digesters open nearby; if they halve, the NPV becomes −$4.2M. The project breaks even if gate fees stay above about 86% of today's level. Sign 10-year waste contracts and use more of the co-op's own manure before committing. Next step: approach the three largest food processors.","great":["Computes NPV with the lender's rate","Identifies the riskiest income stream","Finds the break-even gate fee","Makes the decision conditional on contracts"],"id":85,"slug":"fenland-biogas"}